    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW23kXJCStWuF4CuA5pTu6qmU)_\n\n## Problem\n- BibTeX author `Arthur, Christopher J.` gave the title `J. Arthur (2022) Capital as...` instead of `Arthur (2022) ...`.\n\n## Cause\n- `sp-litnotes-titles--split-name` is the one function that finds the surname. The backfill (`sp-litnotes-meta--new-title`), titles report/convert and the BibTeX-authors path all call it.\n- Names are flipped to `First Last` before it runs, so it used its \"particle\" rule: lower-case words before the last word belong to the surname.\n- That test ran with `case-fold-search` on, so the initial `J.` counted as a lower-case particle and went into the surname.\n\n## Change\n- Particles are matched case-sensitively, and only whole lower-case words (`van`, `de la`) count.\n- Commas are split outside braces only: `{Smith, Jones}, Ann` has surname `Smith, Jones`; `Last, Jr., First` has surname `Last`.\n- `{World Bank}` stays one surname; no comma and one word stays as is.\n- Tests (`tests/sp-litnotes-titles-test.el`, `tests/sp-litnotes-meta-test.el`): the forms above, `case-fold-search` on and off, BibTeX authors, and the backfill title. 34/34 pass on Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Not tested\n- Not run on the real vault; existing litnotes already titled `J. Arthur (...)` are not renamed by this PR (re-run the titles convert/report to fix them).\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiATczu45nYqwaKie4g)_",
